From: Vojtech Bubnik <bubnikv@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Harden libusb probing and streaming teardown

Keep exact accounting for partial transfer submissions and drain cancelled
transfers for at most 500 ms. If a wrapped Android fd was closed before the
transfers could be reaped, retain the complete device and USB session rather
than freeing objects still referenced by libusb or the kernel. libhackrf uses
one global context, so retaining the device object is also necessary in case
another HackRF event thread processes a late callback.

Also validate libusb enumeration and string-descriptor results, initialize USB
string buffers, pass Android's no-discovery option through libusb_init_context,
make every hackrf_open_setup failure release partially-created resources, and
recognize the pthreads4w target exported by the SDR++ dependency build.
---
diff --git a/host/libhackrf/src/CMakeLists.txt b/host/libhackrf/src/CMakeLists.txt
index dc21548e..7e0c9ef9 100644
--- a/host/libhackrf/src/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/host/libhackrf/src/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -62,6 +62,8 @@ function(libhackrf_common_settings libtarget)
   target_link_libraries(${libtarget} PRIVATE LIBUSB::LIBUSB)
   if(TARGET PThreads4W::PThreads4W)
     target_link_libraries(${libtarget} PRIVATE PThreads4W::PThreads4W)
+  elseif(TARGET pthreads4w::pthreadVC3)
+    target_link_libraries(${libtarget} PRIVATE pthreads4w::pthreadVC3)
   else()
     target_link_libraries(${libtarget} PRIVATE Threads::Threads)
   endif()
